1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,754
Price made a new high. Everyone was happy and rushed to buy.

2
00:00:10,204 --> 00:00:14,488
But underneath, the buyers in a hurry were getting fewer.

3
00:00:14,937 --> 00:00:21,208
The chart does not show this. CVD does. It is called delta divergence.

4
00:00:22,208 --> 00:00:26,961
Hello, this is episode fourteen of the SPIDER Order Flow series.

5
00:00:27,412 --> 00:00:32,976
Last time: delta and CVD, the running total of delta.

6
00:00:33,426 --> 00:00:39,382
Today: delta divergence. When price says one thing and delta another.

7
00:00:40,382 --> 00:00:47,383
Remember: if price and CVD both make new highs, the trend is healthy.

8
00:00:47,833 --> 00:00:51,229
But sometimes the two take different paths.

9
00:00:51,679 --> 00:00:58,366
Price up, CVD down. Or price down, CVD up. That is divergence.

10
00:00:59,366 --> 00:01:05,636
First: bearish divergence. Price makes a first high at 2650.

11
00:01:06,086 --> 00:01:11,152
Then a new high at 2662. Price went higher.

12
00:01:11,603 --> 00:01:19,309
But CVD was +1200 at the first high and only +800 at the new one. CVD stayed lower.

13
00:01:20,309 --> 00:01:25,142
Meaning: price did go up, but with fewer buyers in a hurry.

14
00:01:25,592 --> 00:01:30,503
Maybe sellers just stepped aside. Or buyers started to tire.

15
00:01:30,952 --> 00:01:36,517
It is a warning, not an entry. The upward push is weakening.

16
00:01:37,517 --> 00:01:40,443
The reverse also happens: bullish divergence.

17
00:01:40,893 --> 00:01:46,378
Price makes a low at 2600, then a new low at 2588.

18
00:01:46,829 --> 00:01:55,187
But CVD was −900 at the first low and only −500 at the new one. The sellers in a hurry are fading.

19
00:01:56,187 --> 00:02:01,256
There is another form: hidden divergence. It shows up in the middle of a trend.

20
00:02:01,705 --> 00:02:08,941
In an uptrend a pullback came. Price held a higher low, at 2620 instead of 2610.

21
00:02:09,390 --> 00:02:22,218
But CVD fell from −300 to −700. Sellers pushed hard, yet price did not fall. Someone was quietly buying below. A hint the trend continues.

22
00:02:23,218 --> 00:02:28,129
Now three examples. Two right, one wrong. Honestly.

23
00:02:28,579 --> 00:02:34,064
One: a bearish divergence formed at yesterday's high of 2662.

24
00:02:34,513 --> 00:02:43,344
Then price broke its last swing low at 2648. Only then did the drop start, down to 2630.

25
00:02:44,344 --> 00:02:49,986
Two: a bullish divergence at the Value Area Low of 2588.

26
00:02:50,436 --> 00:02:55,112
Price made a new low, but the sellers in a hurry were pulling back.

27
00:02:55,561 --> 00:03:01,204
Price came back into value and reached the POC at 2605.

28
00:03:02,204 --> 00:03:05,364
Three: a strong trend day.

29
00:03:05,815 --> 00:03:12,162
Three bearish divergences formed one after another. Each time it looked like price would fall.

30
00:03:12,613 --> 00:03:22,174
But price kept climbing, from 2650 to 2700. Anyone selling every divergence was stopped out three times.

31
00:03:23,174 --> 00:03:25,290
So when is divergence useful?

32
00:03:25,739 --> 00:03:32,976
When it forms at an important level: yesterday's high or low, the edges of the Value Area, or another big level.

33
00:03:33,426 --> 00:03:43,143
And when price confirms it, for example by breaking its last swing. On strong trend or big news days, divergence is often false.

34
00:03:44,143 --> 00:03:49,786
And the same truth again: spot forex and gold have no real CVD.

35
00:03:50,236 --> 00:03:57,707
CVD indicators on MT5 estimate from ticks. A divergence then becomes an estimate of an estimate.

36
00:03:58,156 --> 00:04:04,426
Real CVD comes from futures: gold futures, currency futures or a crypto exchange.

37
00:04:05,426 --> 00:04:06,993
So, today's summary.

38
00:04:07,442 --> 00:04:16,691
Divergence: price and CVD split. Bearish: price higher, CVD lower. Bullish: the reverse.

39
00:04:17,141 --> 00:04:22,705
Hidden divergence appears mid-trend and hints the trend continues.

40
00:04:23,155 --> 00:04:30,391
Divergence is a warning, not an entry. Useful only with a key level and price confirmation.

41
00:04:31,391 --> 00:04:38,157
Next episode: imbalance and stacked imbalance. Where one side pushed hard.

42
00:04:38,607 --> 00:04:43,518
